      "content": "The desire to avoid feeling the full weight of your pain is completely understandable, though try not to see avoiding the bottom as a skill to master, but rather a privilege of survival. When you stop fighting to be a \"person of worth\" in the chaos, you often actually gain a strange, quiet control over how you act and feel in the world, even if the pain remains. You are not responsible for everyone else's judgment, and while waiting for the impact feels inevitable, it is also tiring and unnecessary to do so if professional support can help you create a small container for that feeling rather than letting it spill everywhere immediately.",
